@startuml browser_masquerade_sequence
' Browser masquerade search + crawl workflow, measured 2026-10-19.
' 6 lanes on Xvfb :99-:104, distro Firefox 157 (feat/distro-firefox-fleet),
' Thai residential egress. Google engine re-enabled; brave back after the
' IIFE payload fix (see git log 2026-10-19). 2026-10-20: google images
' switched from the discontinued WML endpoint to the desktop image grid,
' served by the same human flow from /imghp (imgres+tiles parser; the
' 2026-10-20 run: 50 results, 21-35 s warm lane).

autonumber

participant "Onyx\n(web_search / open_url)" as Onyx
participant "searxng\nwebapp" as Web
participant "engine module\n(google/bing/brave/...)" as Eng
participant "BrowserFetchPool\n(6 lanes)" as Pool
participant "lane N\nFirefox on Xvfb" as Lane
participant "human_input\n(XTEST pointer)" as Hand
participant "captcha_vision\n(OpenAI-compatible\nvision endpoint)" as Vision
participant "provider\n(google.com, brave,\bbing, ...)" as Up

Onyx -> Web : GET /search?q=... (json)
note right of Onyx : Onyx client read budget 450 s = 2x worst\nattempt (SEARXNG_READ_TIMEOUT_SECONDS);\nretries paced 20 s / 40 s like a person\nre-querying

Web -> Eng : engine request
Eng -> Pool : fetch(url) via browser pool
note right of Pool : provider send pacing:\n1-5 s random gap per host,\nqueue cap 20 s

Pool -> Pool : checkout next idle lane\n(asyncio lane cycle)
note right of Pool : lane displays :99-:104 are self-healing\n(2026-10-19): stale X locks are cleaned only\nwhen the lock's PID does not name THIS display\n(PID reuse after restart poisoned the old\ncheck), and a spawned Xvfb is verified --\nsocket newer than pre-spawn, process alive,\nsomething listens -- with one clean+retry\nround before headless fallback
note right of Pool : per-origin human pacing on the\nbrowser lanes:\nsame origin keeps a jittered min gap\n-- search engines 4-10 s, other sites\n8-20 s, burst cap 45 s -- across all\nlanes, like one attentive person;\ndifferent origins stay parallel
note right of Pool : wait here if all 6 lanes busy,\nbounded: 20 s, then the oldest\nbackground browsing session is\ncancelled, then up to 90 s more\n(engine timeout budget:\ngoogle 100 s, others 75-90 s)

alt maximum stealth (browser_max_stealth: on)
    Pool -> Lane : open provider homepage\n(vertical front page: google web ->\ngoogle.com, google images -> /imghp --\nits search box submits into the\nvertical; hl/gl locale params ride along;\nno uBlock: google sees the whole jar,\nSERP ad anchors included)
    Lane -> Up : GET homepage
    Hand -> Lane : Bezier move to search box (0.04-0.10 s),\nreal click focuses the box
    Hand -> Lane : type query with human cadence\n(uneven keys, bursts, pauses)
    Hand -> Lane : drift pointer (0.4-1.4 s),\nclick the submit button
    Lane -> Up : form submit -> results page\n(google's form lands on its own\nvertical: /search udm=2 for images)
    Pool -> Lane : settle: wait for navigation,\nread results like a human
    note right of Pool : warm-lane searches measured\n~20-40 s (google), ~20-25 s (brave);\nan images grid gets one extra\nviewport of scroll so its lazy\ntiles paint before capture

    opt google: reCAPTCHA Enterprise (checkbox -> image grid)
        Hand -> Lane : click the challenge checkbox\n(iframe recaptcha/enterprise/anchor)
        Lane -> Up : grid mounts (9-16 tiles, instruction\nin the lane's locale -- Thai)
        loop up to 12 rounds (max_rounds)
            Lane -> Vision : row strips + prompt; ONE vote\ndecides (votes: 1, no inverted\nquorum); endpoint timeout 360 s
            Vision --> Lane : tile coordinates
            Hand -> Lane : click tiles, dwell like a person\n(30-70 s observed), press VERIFY
            opt slide accepted -> next grid
                Lane -> Lane : next round, adapted geometry
            end
        end
        note right of Lane : 2026-10-19: slide-1 clears happen\n(cleared in 57 s -> results in 80 s),\nbut flagged jars mostly get rejected\nand escalated. A request waiting on a\nsolve gives up at its engine timeout\n(100 s); the lane keeps solving up to\nsession_budget 1500 s in the\nbackground and banks the clearance\n+ GOOGLE_ABUSE_EXEMPTION cookie
    else brave: own /captcha challenge (no third-party widget)
        Pool -> Lane : wait out the invisible PoW\n(self-clears and reloads the search)
        opt PoW refused -> slider puzzle
            Hand -> Lane : drag the knob with real X input
            opt end-drags refused
                Lane -> Vision : slider screenshot + prompt\n(vision fallback)
                Vision --> Lane : target position
                Hand -> Lane : drag to the vision answer
            end
        end
    end

    Pool -> Lane : capture rendered DOM (provider desktop layout)
    Lane --> Pool : HTML (~0.3-2.9 MB)
    Pool --> Eng : response
    Eng -> Eng : parse results\n(google /goto?url= kept; brave IIFE\nhydration payload unwrapped -- legacy\ndata: [{...}] still supported)

else not a human-search candidate (API endpoints, ddg)
    Pool -> Lane : fetch-style request in browser context\n(browser TLS + lane cookies)
    Lane -> Up : GET url
    Lane --> Pool : response
end

opt post-search browsing (browser_post_search_browsing)\nscheduler: search > crawl > browsing -- skipped when\nwork is pending, preempted by affinity crawls
    Pool -> Lane : background task keeps the SERP page
    loop 1-4 visits, budget 180 s total
        Hand -> Lane : click an organic result\n(/goto wrapper -> new tab; never\ntranslate.goog targets)
        Lane -> Up : navigate to result
        Hand -> Lane : scroll + pointer drift, dwell 10-30 s
        Lane -> Lane : close tab, back on results
    end
    note right of Lane : measured: 1 visit in 126 s\n(2026-10-19, busy pool)
    Lane --> Pool : lane returns to the cycle
end

Pool --> Web : parsed results
Web --> Onyx : json (warm lane ~20-40 s;\nchallenged google: 80-100 s or a\ntimeout while the lane banks the\nclearance)

== page crawls (Onyx open_url -> /crawl) ==

Onyx -> Web : GET /crawl?url=...
Web -> Pool : crawl_render(url)
Pool -> Pool : affinity: the lane whose SERP\nreturned this URL (memory: last\n600 result URLs per lane)
note right of Pool : search-engine wrapper links\n(google /goto?url=, /url?q=,\nbing /ck/a, ddg /l/?uddg, yahoo /r/)\nare REFUSED when no lane memory\nholds the minting SERP: the tokens\nare bound to the jar the SERP was\nserved to -- another jar following\none is a cross-jar correlation\nhanded straight to the engine

alt affinity lane free
    Pool -> Lane : crawl on the finding lane\n(same identity that found the link)
else affinity lane busy mid-request
    Pool -> Lane : ride the busy lane (a reader\nwith many tabs, same jar)
else no memory hit, a lane free
    Pool -> Lane : crawl on any free lane\n(publisher pages only: wrapper\nlinks would have been refused)
else no memory hit, all lanes busy
    Pool -> Lane : borrow any alive lane\n(last resort)
end
Pool -> Lane : open page with the crawl filter:\nthird-party ad/metric networks\n(taboola, outbrain, criteo, adnxs, ...)\nand video media aborted; google's own\npipeline (googlesyndication,\ndoubleclick, GA, GTM) loads -- it is\nthe cross-site jar signal
Lane -> Up : GET url (follows redirects)
Lane --> Pool : rendered DOM
Pool --> Web : {final_url, status, html, lane}
Web --> Onyx : crawl result

note over Pool, Lane : engine-level rate limits surface as a clean\n1 h suspension (searxng suspension state) --\nnever a crashed search thread: the\nTooManyRequestsException carries its message\nin the message= slot and a guard in\nprocessors/abstract.py nulls non-numeric\nsuspended_time values from any engine
@enduml
